---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="RNN vs Transformer | Ravikumar Buragapu"
			description="A parameter-matched comparison of vanilla RNN, LSTM, GRU, and a tiny Transformer on character language modeling and long-range recall."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<p>RESEARCH PROTOTYPE · SEQUENCE MODELS · CONTROLLED COMPARISON</p>
			<h1>RNN vs LSTM vs GRU vs Tiny Transformer</h1>
			<p>
				At small scale, does attention beat recurrence—or mainly
				change the compute bill? This experiment approximately
				matches model parameter counts, compares character-level
				language modeling, and probes recall across 100 distractor
				steps.
			</p>

			<section aria-labelledby="comparison">
				<h2 id="comparison">One budget, four architectures</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>Vanilla RNN, LSTM, and GRU against a two-layer, four-head causal Transformer.</li>
					<li>Validation loss vs training steps and perplexity.</li>
					<li>200-character samples and per-epoch training time.</li>
					<li>Autoregressive inference tokens/second and latency.</li>
					<li>Synthetic long-range recall with a 50% random baseline.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					The bundled corpus and recall probe are intentionally
					small. Results depend on training budget and hardware;
					this is a reproducible experiment, not a universal
					architecture ranking.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="run">
				<h2 id="run">Run the comparison</h2>
				<pre><code>cd sequence-models
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
sequence-models
pytest</code></pre>
				<p>
					<a href="https://github.com/buragapuravi/my_research_work/tree/main/sequence-models"
						>Read the project README</a
					>
					·
					<a href="/projects/tokenizer-ablation">Explore Tokenizer Ablation</a>
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
